  ],
  "description": "Mäag EQ4-500 from the early hardware manual and Clifford Maag and Lance Parker’s US5717773 figures 1 and 3. Parallel non-inverting RC decks carry the overlap and fixed through-level described in the patent. Four fixed bells, a 2.5 kHz shelf, and five selectable Air shelf frequencies feed one summing amplifier. Air gain also lifts the shared through-level. The highest selected Air frequency wins; with all frequency switches off the 2.5 kHz Air setting applies. The production component list is unverified. Component values are calibrated, linear band op amps and a rail-limited NE5532 line driver approximate the amplifier behavior, and continuous controls stand in for the factory gain detents. Measured full-cut depth varies by band. Extreme line-driver clipping can cause solver step rejection.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Sub 10 Hz Gain",
      "40 Hz Gain",
      "160 Hz Gain",
      "650 Hz Gain",
      "2.5 kHz Gain",
      "Air Gain"
    ],
    "switches": [
      "Air 5 kHz",
      "Air 10 kHz",
      "Air 20 kHz",
      "Air 40 kHz",
      "Air Off",
      "EQ Bypass"
    ]
  },
  "name": "Mäag EQ4-500 Parallel Circuit Model",
